*.swp

# npm is not used here; pnpm-lock.yaml is the lockfile. This file is a stub from
# before the workspace existed.
package-lock.json

# NOTE: packages/app/src/routeTree.gen.ts is NOT ignored, even though the TanStack
# Router Vite plugin generates it from packages/app/src/routes. It is committed on
# purpose, for two reasons:
#
#   1. `pnpm typecheck` runs `tsc` with no Vite plugin in the process, so on a
#      fresh clone it fails with TS2307 unless the file already exists. Committing
#      it keeps a clean checkout green without a build first.
#   2. A route tree that only exists after a build hides real type errors in
#      route files, because the stale tree describes the routes as they were.
#
# The plugin regenerates it on every dev server start, test run and build, and the
# output is deterministic, so a stale copy is never committed by accident: adding
# or renaming a route changes the file and shows up in `git diff`.
#
# It stays in .prettierignore so formatting never rewrites generated output.
